Feature: A hovering plane on its own
  The T1-S VTOL and the Seeker 3 quadcopter need no ground station. The sim starts ArduPilot for itself, and the keyboard
  or a radio flies the plane through it: the sticks go to ArduPilot as the radio signals of a
  real receiver. B is the arm switch and N picks the next mode of the radio, and the first is QHOVER on both
  planes. [[Your first hover]] shows each step.

  Expectation: Arming lets ArduPilot run the motors
    ArduPilot arms the plane when the arm switch is on and the throttle is closed. The top
    line of the HUD says ARMED when it has.
    Given the autopilot is disarmed
    When the pilot arms the plane
    Then the autopilot is armed

  Expectation: Opening the throttle lifts the plane straight up
    In QHOVER the plane takes off vertically. There is no throw.
    Given the autopilot is armed
    When the pilot opens the throttle to climb
    Then the plane is flying

  Expectation: Closing the throttle holds the hover
    In the hover modes the middle of the throttle stick holds the height, and the keyboard
    sends the middle when the throttle is closed. The plane does not fall.
    Overrides: A lowered throttle stick brings the plane down
    Given the autopilot is armed
    And the plane is flying
    When the pilot closes the throttle
    Then the plane is flying

  Expectation: Sending the plane home lands it
    In QRTL (a button of the radio on both planes) the plane flies back to the pilot box and lands by itself.
    Given the autopilot is armed
    And the plane is flying
    When the pilot sends the plane home
    Then the plane is on the ground
